  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Detailed drawings/full particulars of the proposed development showing the matters set out below must be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority, in writing, before the relevant parts of the works are commenced. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the details thus approved which shall be implemented in full prior to the first use/occupation of the development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;a)&amp;nbsp; 1:20 elevations of the proposed windows showing the pane pattern and 1:5 sections showing the materials, glazing bars, frames and glazing units.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;b)&amp;nbsp; Full details of the architraves, pilasters and corbelling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;c) Details of the brick bond, mortar and proposed joins to the original building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure that the external appearance of the building is satisfactory and does not detract from the character and visual amenity of the Victoria Park Conservation Area.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;All new works, and works of making good to the retained fabric, whether internal or external (excluding the UPVC windows), shall be finished to match the original work with regard to the methods used and to material, dimensions, composition, form, colour, finish and profile, and in the case of brickwork, facebond and pointing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure that the development respects the character and appearance of the Victoria Park Conservation Area.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
